      "examId": "m2014_socialg11u9_melmeja",
      "number": 1,
      "questionType": "single_choice",
      "questionText": "One special perfume costs a cosmetic shop Birr 2,100. If the shop desires a 25% markup rate based on the selling price, then which one of the following should be set as a selling price for this perfume?",
      "options": [
        "Birr 2,300",
        "Birr 2,400",
        "Birr 2,600",
        "Birr 2,800"
      ],
      "correctAnswerIndex": 3,
      "explanation": "The problem asks for a **markup rate based on the selling price (S)**, which is the markup percentage of the final price.\n\n**Given:**\nCost (C) = Birr 2,100\nMarkup Rate (M) based on S = 25% or 0.25\n\n**Formula:**\n$\\\\text{Selling Price (S)} = \\\\text{Cost (C)} + \\\\text{Markup Amount (A)}$\nSince the Markup Amount is $25\\%$ of the Selling Price, $A = 0.25 S$.\n\n$S = C + 0.25 S$\n$S - 0.25 S = C$\n$0.75 S = 2,100$\n$S = \\\\frac{2,100}{0.75} = \\\\frac{2,100}{\\\\frac{3}{4}} = 2,100 \\\\times \\\\frac{4}{3} = 700 \\\\times 4 = 2,800 \\text{ Birr}$\n\nThe selling price should be Birr 2,800.",
      "topic": "Mathematics"
    },
